REQUIRED DATA-TESTID ATTRIBUTES
-------------------------------
The following data-testid attributes are REQUIRED in the dashboard page implementation:

Page Container:
- [data-testid="dashboard-page"] - Main dashboard container

Dashboard Components:
- [data-testid="quick-insight-card"] - Insight card component
- [data-testid="streak-display"] - Streak counter component
- [data-testid="weekly-summary-card"] - Weekly summary component
- [data-testid="trend-indicator"] - Trend indicator component
- [data-testid="quick-action-buttons"] - Quick action buttons container
- [data-testid="recent-entries-list"] - Recent entries list component

Recent Entries:
- [data-testid="entry-{id}"] - Individual entry items (pattern)

ARIA Structure Required:
- Main container: role="main" aria-label="Dashboard"
- Loading state: role="status" aria-live="polite" with "Loading dashboard..." text
- Quick Actions section: aria-labelledby="quick-actions-heading"
  - <h2 id="quick-actions-heading" class="sr-only">Quick Actions</h2>
- Recent Activity section: aria-labelledby="recent-activity-heading"
  - <h2 id="recent-activity-heading" class="sr-only">Recent Activity</h2>

Interactive Elements:
- All buttons must be proper <button> elements
- "Log Headache" button navigates to /log
- "Quick Check-in" button navigates to /checkin
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible

TEST EXECUTION NOTES
-------------------

To run these tests:

```bash
# Run all E2E tests
pnpm exec playwright test

# Run only dashboard tests
pnpm exec playwright test test/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts

# Run with UI mode for debugging
pnpm exec playwright test --ui

# Run specific test by name
pnpm exec playwright test -g "should display all 6 main components"

# Run on specific browser
pnpm exec playwright test --project="Desktop Chrome"

# Run on mobile viewport only
pnpm exec playwright test --project="iPhone SE"
```

Expected Test Results:
- All tests should pass once data-testid attributes are added to page
- Tests verify real data flow through IndexedDB
- Tests are reliable and not flaky (no hardcoded waits beyond data loading)

